 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-10-26 (17): satchel restyle: grey stone GUI-pack look, flat text, touching slots, a brown book (**NOT b1.7.3**; written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device; +4 tests in `satchel.rs`: `slots_touch_and_sit_clear_of_the_border`, `the_result_stays_on_the_page_on_every_screen`, `the_book_is_as_tall_closed_as_open`, `text_is_fitted_and_wrapped_within_its_box`; run `cargo test --lib satchel hud` first). Player's report on (16): the text looked doubled and ran out of its boxes, the bag's slots were too big and covered the seam on the left, the look was Pixel RPG Fantasy and flat, and the result slot of the book's grid left the page. The sprite sheet was previewed first (`python3 tools/gen_satchel_ui.py --preview DIR` writes the sheet and two mock screens with the game's font); `--write` writes `assets/satchel.rgba`.
+    - Text (`satchel.rs`): `HudPipeline::push_text_flat` (no shadow, origin snapped to whole pixels) replaces `push_text` / `push_text_centered` on the satchel; the old shadow, one font pixel down-right in a quarter of the ink, read as a second copy on parchment. `units(k)` rounds the title / button size (0.75 k) and the small size (0.6 k) to whole pixels, so a glyph and a sprite pixel (`u`) are whole screen pixels (the `tk * 0.85` card head is gone). `fitted` steps a text down whole pixels, then cuts it with a dot; `text_fit` (left edge + width), `text_in` (centred, kept inside `[lo, hi]`), `paragraph` / `lines` (wrapped, cut at the foot) are used for every label, title, button, row, card line and toggle.
+    - Slots: cells touch (pitch = cell, like the vanilla texture) and are `floor`ed to whole pixels; `pad` = max(0.03 h, 11 sprite pixels) because the panel's border is 8 sprite pixels and its seam and corner marks lie inside 7 (the old 0.03 h was less than that at the phone's scale, so the cells covered the seam); the pocket bands are one per block (armor row, the 3 rows, the belt), 2 sprite pixels wider than it; blocks are `6 u` apart; no buckle. The crafting grid's cells touch too.
+    - Grid on the page: a cell is `min(height's share, (page width left of the content - 2 gaps - arrow) / (grid width + 1.2))`, so the result never leaves the page (before, a cell came from the height and the page from the width: at 1920 x 1080 the 2x2 result stuck out by 84 px, 3x3 at 1604 x 720 by 4 px). `BookFrame::p` / `hh` carry the page clearance (`max(0.028 h, 8 u)`, the frame is 6 u) to the drawing.
